  "source": "Alpaca Trading API (orders, account activities, portfolio history) and Alpaca Market Data (IEX feed) pulled 2026-11-21; order, client, and asset identifiers removed",
  "headline": "Week 1 of daily paper trading closed up $273.67 (+4.53%) on a $6,046.91 starting book, ahead of SPY (+2.57%) and QQQ (+3.61%). The book traded 23 round trips across 20 symbols, winning 12 of them; a 1.94 profit factor came from a few large winners (MRVL, CEG, TER, OKLO) outrunning many small losers. The two red days, Thursday and Friday, were driven by a two-night hold in TEM that gapped down and a cluster of tight bracket stops in EAT.",
  "day_notes": {
   "2026-11-09": "Clean intraday test: four names bought between 9:52 and 11:50 AM, all four flattened between 3:07 and 3:09 PM. CEG (+$141.92) and OKLO (+$71.88) carried the day while NVDA and ABNB lost $26 combined. A 0.0004-share LITE remnant from the October book was also cleaned up.",
   "2026-11-10": "First overnight holds of the test. NET was sold at 3:51 PM for +$52.17, but NRC, JNJ and MRVL were carried into Wednesday, so the day's equity gain includes their mark-to-market rather than only realized P&L.",
   "2026-11-11": "Best day of the week. Six names opened in the first 90 minutes, then the whole book except TEM was flattened between 2:48 and 2:53 PM. MRVL, held from Tuesday, produced +$155.10, the week's largest winner, and TER added +$78.20. Seven of eight round trips were profitable. TEM was carried overnight.",
   "2026-11-12": "Six new names at the open. TSLA was cut 28 minutes after entry for -$41.29 and AAPL lost -$43.34 into the close; GOOGL (+$33.25) was the only meaningful winner. Two of six round trips won. TEM was held a second night.",
   "2026-11-13": "TEM gapped down and the OCO stop at $71.40 fired at 9:33 AM for -$124.00 (-14.8%), the worst trade of the week and the cost of two nights of exposure. The rest of the session was three EAT attempts with OCO brackets (10 long, 5 long, 5 short), all stopped within minutes to an hour for a combined -$30.69. First use of brackets and the first short of the test. A $3,000 paper deposit landed at 11:34 AM and is excluded from every figure here."
  },
  "context_before": "From Oct 20 to Nov 6 the same paper account ran a very different, concentrated book (FICO, SNDK, LITE, including fractional shares on margin). Equity fell from about $36,000 on Oct 28 to $6,046.90 at the Nov 6 close, roughly -83%, and $210.03 of margin interest was charged on Nov 2. A $3,000 paper deposit on Nov 3 is inside that window. Week 1 of the daily test therefore started on Nov 9 from a flat book and a $6,046.91 base.",
  "context_after": "Since week 1 the cadence has been lighter: Nov 16 traded SPOT (stopped at breakeven, -$0.09) and TM (-$25.33); Nov 17 to 19 had no fills; Nov 20 bought INTU (19 sh), FICO (20 sh, closed +$404.60) and EPAM (closed +$23.59). INTU was still open when this report was pulled, showing -$316.47 unrealized against account equity of $9,368.67.",
  "lessons": [
   "Intraday round trips did the work: 19 same-day trades netted +$254.84 (10 winners), while the 4 overnight holds netted only +$19.80 with a wide spread (MRVL +$155.10 versus TEM -$124.00). Overnight exposure added variance, not edge.",
   "The win rate was 52% but the profit factor was 1.94 because the average winner ($47.23) was 1.8x the average loser ($26.55). The edge this week came from letting CEG, TER, OKLO and MRVL run, not from being right often.",
   "Sizing was a flat 10 shares (25 for OKLO, 50 for VSTM) regardless of price, so notional per trade ranged from $267 to $3,941. Risk per trade was uncontrolled; TSLA and AAPL at ~$3,500 to $3,900 notional were the two largest intraday losers.",
   "Every one of the 49 week-1 orders was entered by hand: 43 through the Alpaca web dashboard and 6 through an API key for the OCO brackets. This was a human-in-the-loop test of the signals, not an autonomous bot run, so execution timing (first fills 9:32 to 11:50 AM, exits clustered 2:48 to 3:51 PM) reflects the operator's schedule.",
   "OCO brackets were introduced only on Friday. All five stop legs that could trigger did trigger, at 1% to 2% below entry on EAT, which suggests the stops were inside normal intraday noise for a $200 stock with a 3% daily range.",
   "Fees were immaterial on paper ($0.97 of REG and CAT fees for the week) but the margin interest charged in late October (-$210.03) is a reminder that the account is running 4x buying power."
  ],
  "next_steps": [
   "Move to equal-notional or ATR-based sizing (for example 5% of equity per position, which at ~$6,300 is about $315) so every trade risks roughly the same amount.",
   "Default to flat-by-close; if a position is carried overnight, it must carry a stop. The TEM hold had no stop until Friday morning.",
   "Attach an OCO bracket to every entry but set the stop from the 14-day ATR (roughly 1.0 to 1.5 ATR) rather than a fixed percentage.",
   "Log the signal that produced each entry (Depot Score, Momentum Pro, or discretionary) at order time so week 2's report can attribute P&L by strategy.",
   "Keep deposits out of performance by recording them as they happen; this report subtracts them automatically from the equity curve.",
   "Regenerate this report every Friday after the close from a fresh Alpaca pull using scripts/weekly_paper_report.py."
  ]
